! mcp_bootstrap_p250.strap -- MCP printed page 250: the Input Program's
! card-reader recovery section, continued (LV,$9,RRCCW .. LWF(U),RNLJAM),
! lines 1-56: RRCCW, RCREJB, RSAM, RCNXRJ, RK1000, the two UK messages
! RBFFUK / RCMMUK, RCOMMK, RTONRJ, RSONO, RPTCOM.
!
! docs/MCP_Mar63_250-445.pdf PDF p.1 (volume 2's first page), read at
! 400 dpi, 900 dpi for doubtful glyphs.  Header, READ: "TIME CLOCK
! 00054041  PUNID 11D11MCP  CARD ID CB000295  DIST. OF 3/01  3/01  PAGE
! NUMBER 250" (round glyphs in numeric fields read 0); the heading
! row's LOCATION field is 230106, line 1's word.
!
! THE PAGE.  56 lines, all located, contiguous from 230106.40 to
! 230157.00 (a half word; next location 230157.40), then blank paper.
! p.249 ends with a half word at 230106.00 (,VCREXT), so line 1's .40
! continues it.  Line 3 (TI) is a full word 230107.40..230110.40; lines
! 26-28 (BB, TBI, TI), 45-46 (BZB1, BB1) and 48 (ST) are full words.
! Line 5 is an XW at 230111.00.  Line 39 (A*)DD 32 characters = 4
! words, 230134.00..230137.77; line 40 (IQS*)DD 48 characters = 6
! words, 230140.00..230145.77.  Every line number prints with an
! asterisk after it ("1*" .. "56*"); asterisks after the LOCATION on
! lines 8, 28, 40 and 53.  No remark column on this page.
!
! GLYPHS SETTLED BY OTHER THAN PLAIN INK:
!   * line 3 "RDLEOF": the L's foot is faint at 900 dpi (reads I); TI
!     prints 230411.00, external, value from this page only.
!   * line 5 "XW,C.32,0" = XW,0.32,0 (open round, as p.249's SYN note
!     reads it); XW prints 000000.40+.
!   * line 22 "$19" (9 struck over 5): written $15 -- KVI prints
!     225176.77, J 15, as line 24's KVI,$15 prints .77; $19 is no index.
!   * line 24 "VSECJ" = VSEOJ (open O): landed p.224 VSEOJ 224600.40,
!     C22-6728 spells VSEOJ (13), VSECJ nowhere; KVI prints 224602.77.
!   * line 26 "RCOMMK" (closed O) vs line 41 label printed "RCCMMK"
!     (open): one symbol, B line 26 prints 230146.34 = line 41's
!     230146.00; the closed O decides, written RCOMMK both places.
!   * line 23 "RSONO" (closed third glyph, squared like this page's
!     closed O in RCOMMK, RK1000) vs line 46 label printed "RSCNO"
!     (open): one symbol, BXE line 23 prints 230151.32 = line 46's
!     230151.00; written RSONO.  No deck, neighbour or manual spells it.
!   * line 42 ",$CCMM" = ,$COMM (worn O): the pseudo-op system symbol;
!     prints 000043.40.
!   * line 36 ",$ECJ" = ,$EOJ (open O): MCP pseudo-op EOJ, printed p.105
!     line 33 = 65 = 000101.00 as this row prints; C28-6129's own
!     example is ", $EOJ".  $ECJ is no system symbol.
!   * line 46 "REJJCB" = REJJOB (as line 45, and as landed decks).
!   * line 52 "VCCM" / line 55 "VCOM": VCOM as landed (224702.0).
!   * line 48 byte "DC" = D0 (ST, as p.217 line 24's ST(BU,32) prints
!     "DC" and assembles D0; no offset index in the statement).
!   * line 28 byte "AC" = A0: the same row prints ".1C" in an octal
!     field (so open rounds are 0 here), and the statement names no
!     offset index, so the low nibble i2 is 0; assembles A0 (line 27's
!     TBI prints A0 closed).
!   * hex bytes printed with an open round written 0 ("C0" lines 2, 8,
!     ...; "C4" line 24 = 04; "C1" etc.), octal fields "CCCCCC.CC" are
!     0.  "C2" lines 20, 23, 25 (BXE) and "C8" lines 18, 49 (CB-) are C
!     (they assemble so, as p.249's BXE prints C2).
!
! CARD SERIALS.  Right-hand serials run 0B000295 .. 0B000326 (prefix
